1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Whining noise from under the hood
when you rev the engine?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Sounds like the belt.
It might not be.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
One clue: a worn alternator bearing can
whine at the exact same pitch as belt slip.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Keep driving on it and the alternator
can seize — and take the belt with it.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Don't guess which part is whining.
A quick listening test narrows it down.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Worth checking before a seized pulley
strands you. Stop by — Nick's Tire & Auto.
